{"name":"Abel","hex":"#f5ecda","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Abel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The son of Adam and Eve who was killed by his brother Cain.","A male given name from Hebrew."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Abel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Abel","blocks":[{"text":"Abel is a biblical figure in the Book of Genesis within the Abrahamic religions. Born as the second son of Adam and Eve, the first two humans created by God, he was a shepherd who offered his firstborn flock to God as a religious offering. God accepted Abel's offering but not that of his older brother Cain, leading Cain to kill Abel out of jealousy; some later interpretations suggest that Cain may have slain him with a stone. This act marked the first death in biblical history, making Abel the first murder victim."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Sacrificio_de_Abel%2C_de_Juan_Antonio_de_Fr%C3%ADas_y_Escalante_%28Museo_del_Prado%29.jpg/330px-Sacrificio_de_Abel%2C_de_Juan_Antonio_de_Fr%C3%ADas_y_Escalante_%28Museo_del_Prado%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abel"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Cain_leadeth_abel_to_death_tissot.jpg/500px-Cain_leadeth_abel_to_death_tissot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Cain_leadeth_abel_to_death_tissot.jpg/1280px-Cain_leadeth_abel_to_death_tissot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Cain_leadeth_abel_to_death_tissot.jpg/500px-Cain_leadeth_abel_to_death_tissot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cain leadeth Abel to death, by James Tissot, c. 1900","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fil